From 1f6db6453b359574a1436ce8e988460e143e7262 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:29:52 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/32] kcm_desktoppaths: Form page ordered by use, plain
 FormLayout rows instead of Kirigami.Form

Page type: Form (docs/page-design.md). Settings keys, user-dirs.dirs handling, defaults unchanged. Not built yet.

Moved / renamed:
- Order: Downloads, Documents, Desktop, Pictures, Music, Videos first (untitled section); Public, Templates, Projects in a
  second section "Sharing and Development" (kcm_desktoppaths/Public, Templates, Projects). Labels unchanged.
- UrlRequester is now a RowLayout (read-only path field + folder button) used as a FormLayout row instead of a
  Kirigami.FormEntry in Form/FormGroup with a SizeGroup; the default-differs highlight targets the text field.
- Path field and button get Accessible.name/description (kcm_desktoppaths/Choose-new-location).
- Shell name is "Personal Folders" (ia/layout.json), "Locations" stays an alias there.
HIG ids: HIG-001/005 (order by use), HIG-057 (section title is a noun).

Speed cause: nothing blocking in the page; the cost was nine FormEntry items (each builds title, subtitle, trailing items and a
layout) plus a Kirigami.SizeGroup over their content items. Plain rows remove that. user-dirs.dirs is read in the
settings constructor (small file, kept). After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Unconfirmed: KCM.SettingHighlighter `target` set to the TextField (property exists in kcmutils settinghighlighterprivate.h).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
